<para>CARR_VEC_OutOfBounds if <computeroutput>idx</computeroutput> is invalid. </para>

<para>CARR_VEC_NULL if a required pointer is NULL.</para>
</formalpara>
<note><title>Note</title>

<para>This function replaces the stored pointer. Ownership and cleanup of the previous element are determined by the implementation. </para>
</note>
</para>
<para>
References <link linkend="_carr_8h_1af4e0864f9b23847ec5128bed12c16cf4">carr_replaceIndex()</link>.</para>
<para>
Referenced by <link linkend="_carr_8h_1af4e0864f9b23847ec5128bed12c16cf4">carr_replaceIndex()</link>.</para>
</section>
<anchor xml:id="_carr_8h_1a73fa03395af35a5b22ade60714a7a104"/><section>
    <title>carr_resize()</title>
<indexterm><primary>carr_resize</primary><secondary>carr.h</secondary></indexterm>
<indexterm><primary>carr.h</primary><secondary>carr_resize</secondary></indexterm>
<para><computeroutput><link linkend="_carr_8h_1ab4bdc8444943761b4337de9fe5b718ec">CARRError</link> carr_resize (<link linkend="_structCARR">CARR</link> * vec, const size_t newCap)</computeroutput></para><para>

<para>Changes the capacity of a vector. </para>
</para>

<para>Requests a new capacity for the vector&apos;s underlying pointer array.</para>

<para>
                <formalpara>
                    <title>
Parameters</title>
                    <para>
                    <table frame="all">
                        <tgroup cols="3" align="left" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
                        <colspec colwidth="1*"/>
                        <colspec colwidth="1*"/>
                        <colspec colwidth="4*"/>
                        <tbody>
                            <row>
<entry>in,out</entry><entry>vec</entry><entry>
<para>Pointer to the vector to resize. </para>
</entry>
                            </row>
                            <row>
<entry>in</entry><entry>newCap</entry><entry>
<para>Desired capacity.</para>
</entry>
                            </row>
                        </tbody>
                        </tgroup>
                    </table>
                    </para>
                </formalpara>
                <formalpara><title>Returns</title>

<para>CARR_VEC_OK if successful. </para>

<para>CARR_VEC_NULL if a required pointer is NULL. </para>

<para>CARR_VEC_ResizeError if resizing fails or is not permitted. </para>

<para>CARR_VEC_OOM if memory allocation fails.</para>
</formalpara>
<note><title>Note</title>

<para>The exact behavior when <computeroutput>newCap</computeroutput> is smaller than the current size depends on the implementation. </para>
</note>
</para>
<para>
References <link linkend="_carr_8h_1a73fa03395af35a5b22ade60714a7a104">carr_resize()</link>.</para>
<para>
Referenced by <link linkend="_carr_8h_1a73fa03395af35a5b22ade60714a7a104">carr_resize()</link>.</para>
