<anchor xml:id="_carr_8h_1acb108ce8c3e77993b32f071d7f81fe4c"/><section>
    <title>carr_reverse()</title>
<indexterm><primary>carr_reverse</primary><secondary>carr.h</secondary></indexterm>
<indexterm><primary>carr.h</primary><secondary>carr_reverse</secondary></indexterm>
<para><computeroutput><link linkend="_carr_8h_1ab4bdc8444943761b4337de9fe5b718ec">CARRError</link> carr_reverse (<link linkend="_structCARR">CARR</link> * vec)</computeroutput></para><para>

<para>Reverses the order of elements in the vector. </para>
</para>

<para>Reorders the stored pointers so that the first element becomes the last, the second becomes the second-to-last, and so on.</para>

<para>
                <formalpara>
                    <title>
Parameters</title>
                    <para>
                    <table frame="all">
                        <tgroup cols="3" align="left" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
                        <colspec colwidth="1*"/>
                        <colspec colwidth="1*"/>
                        <colspec colwidth="4*"/>
                        <tbody>
                            <row>
<entry>in,out</entry><entry>vec</entry><entry>
<para>Pointer to the vector to reverse.</para>
</entry>
                            </row>
                        </tbody>
                        </tgroup>
                    </table>
                    </para>
                </formalpara>
                <formalpara><title>Returns</title>

<para>CARR_VEC_OK if successful. </para>

<para>CARR_VEC_NULL if a required pointer is NULL.</para>
</formalpara>
<note><title>Note</title>

<para>The elements themselves are not copied or modified; only their positions in the vector are changed. </para>
</note>
</para>
<para>
References <link linkend="_carr_8h_1acb108ce8c3e77993b32f071d7f81fe4c">carr_reverse()</link>.</para>
<para>
Referenced by <link linkend="_carr_8h_1acb108ce8c3e77993b32f071d7f81fe4c">carr_reverse()</link>.</para>
</section>
